---
description: Project coding rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# General

- Use TypeScript only.
- Never use `any`.
- Never break existing APIs.
- Preserve architecture.
- Reuse existing components.
- Prefer composition over duplication.

# React

- Functional components only.
- Keep components small.
- Split large components.

# Next.js

- Use App Router.
- Prefer Server Components.
- Use Client Components only when required.

# Supabase

- Database logic belongs in services.
- Components never call Supabase directly.

# Styling

- TailwindCSS only.
- Reuse existing UI.

# Architecture

- Always analyze before editing.
- Never create duplicate utilities.
- Never create duplicate contexts.

# Refactoring

- Keep behavior unchanged.
- Refactor only requested files.

# AI

Before coding:

1. Read related files.
2. Explain implementation.
3. Then edit.